"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2687,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, who narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Nufayli, who narrated to us Hatim ibn Ismail, who narrated to us Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father (RA), who reported: We entered upon Jabir ibn Abdullah (RA), and he related the full narration, saying: ""It was the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who ordered a hair tent to be set up for himself, so it was pitched for him using a namirah (a tanned animal hide). Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) traveled until he arrived at Arafah, and he found the tent had already been pitched for him with the namirah, so he stayed in it."""
